# This is a fork, not a copy.
#
# It started as the SteamOS CEC Toolkit by Twsts. This project took it at the
# commit above and kept it unchanged in vendor/ for some time. Five functions
# in it did not work on the machines that this project runs on. This project
# corrected each of the five from the outside:
#
#   a unit to register the adapter
#   a drop-in to stop the boot wake from delaying the session
#   a repair step for the permissions race
#   a step to write the physical address that the installer does not write
#   a search for the Bluetooth radios that the USB wake did not find
#
# A tree with five external corrections is not a vendored tree. It is a fork
# with its changes in the wrong repository.
#
# So the fixes are in here now, where the bugs are, and the workarounds are
# gone. See README.md for what changed. The tree is still a module of its own:
# it installs and uninstalls itself, it is managed through
# steamos-cec-toolkitctl, and nothing in this panel is needed to run it.
#
# What was left behind when it was taken, and why:
#
#   decky/   the Game Mode plugin. This panel is the UI here, and the toolkit
#            is managed through steamos-cec-toolkitctl either way - the plugin
#            is one of two front ends for the same helper, not a dependency of
#            it. Nothing in this tree installs it; the docs still mention it
#            where they describe how the pieces fit together.
#
#            There is a decky/ at the top of this repository now, and it is
#            not this one. That is a plugin of this project: it calls
#            steamos-utility-centerctl, and the CEC page of it is one of five.
#            The shape of its backend, and the three environment variables
#            that it corrects, come from the plugin here. decky/main.py says
#            so, and the README credits it.
#   assets/  8.6 MB of screenshots of that plugin.
#
# Taking upstream changes:
#
#   git clone https://github.com/Twsts/steamos-cec-toolkit /tmp/cec
#   git -C /tmp/cec diff v0.1.26 <newer tag> -- bin systemd config udev \
#       wireplumber docs install.sh uninstall.sh VERSION
#
# That diff is what upstream changed since the fork point, so it applies onto
# this tree and shows our own changes as the conflicts. This is worth doing
# and worth not pretending is automatic: the values above are the fork point
# and stay the fork point, because that is what a diff needs. VERSION says
# what this tree is, which is no longer what upstream calls anything.
#
